            <ArticleTitle>Accelerated coronary artery disease in a young woman with pseudoxanthoma elasticum and elevated lipoprotein(a).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1428-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pseudoxanthoma elasticum frequently has cardiovascular involvement. We describe a 29-year-old woman with pseudoxanthoma elasticum and accelerated coronary artery disease who was found to have a highly elevated lipoprotein(a). This unique combination is, most likely, responsible for the clinical presentation of our case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
